__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Simulator work dirs and console logs: regenerable, and large. The convention
# is heteropilot's -- results are committed, the runs that produced them are not.
outputs/
experiments/results/**/work/
*.stdout
*.stderr
# Tool configuration is committed to neither repository (CLAUDE.md, "The
# boundary"). Editor and agent settings live in a global gitignore; these are
# named here too so a stray `git add .` cannot repeat heteropilot #132/#133.
.mcp.json
.ignore
.claude/
.omc/
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/
graft/

# The paper. `tables/` is generated from experiments/results/*.md by
# `make tables` and committing it would let a stale table outlive the markdown
# it came from; the directory itself is kept so `\input` paths resolve before
# the first build. LaTeX's own droppings are regenerable by definition.
paper/tables/*.tex
paper/main.pdf
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.fls
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.synctex.gz
